{"name":"Gecko’s Dream","hex":"#669900","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gecko","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any lizard in the infraorder Gekkota.","Any lizard of the family Gekkonidae of small, carnivorous, mostly nocturnal animals with large eyes and adhesive toes enabling them to climb on vertical and upside-down surfaces."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move in the manner of a gecko; to attach to a vertical or upside-down surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gecko"},{"term":"dream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Imaginary events seen in the mind while sleeping.","A hope or wish."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To see imaginary events in one's mind while sleeping.","To hope, to wish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dream","blocks":[{"text":"A dream is a succession of images, dynamic scenes and situations, ideas, emotions, and sensations that usually occur involuntarily in the mind during certain stages of sleep. Humans generally spend more than two hours dreaming per night, and each dream lasts around 5–20 minutes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg/330px-A_dream_%28BM_1868%2C0808.9057%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dream","wikidata":"Q36348"},{"title":"Gecko","blocks":[{"text":"Geckos are small, mostly carnivorous lizards that have a wide distribution, found on every continent except Antarctica. Belonging to the suborder Gekkota, geckos are found in warm climates. They range from 1.6 to 67 centimetres in length. They are the most species-rich group of lizards, with nearly 2,000 different species of geckos existing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Phelsuma_l._laticauda.jpg/330px-Phelsuma_l._laticauda.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaig